1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,750
You might think that to lose weight you need to do strenuous exercise — like pedalling frantically on an exercise bike or swimming lengths in your local pool.
你可能会认为要减肥就需要进行剧烈的运动——比如在健身单车上拼命地蹬踏，或者在当地的游泳池里来回游泳。

2
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:21,060
But you will be delighted to learn that lying in a steaming hot bath might bring the same benefits as a workout, without all the sweat in the gym!
不过，你可能会惊喜地发现，躺在热气腾腾的浴缸里能带来与运动相同的好处，而且无需在健身房里大汗淋漓！

3
00:00:21,060 --> 00:00:31,260
These were the findings of an experiment comparing the relative benefits of exercise and hot baths that was carried out by Dr Steve Faulkner of Loughborough University.
这些是拉夫堡大学的史蒂夫·福克纳博士进行的一项实验的结果，该实验比较了运动和热水浴的相对益处。

4
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:41,020
The volunteers first lay in a hot bath and then ate a light meal, while their blood sugar level was monitored and the number of calories they burnt was measured.
志愿者们先是躺在热水浴缸里，然后吃了一顿便餐，同时监测他们的血糖水平，并测量他们燃烧的卡路里数量。

5
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:48,930
The experiment was then repeated, but instead of having a bath, the participants did an hour's vigorous exercise on a bike.
然后重复这个实验，但参与者不是泡澡，而是在单车上进行了一个小时的剧烈运动。

6
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:53,840
The results from both activities were compared with unexpected results.
对这两项活动的结果进行了比较，得出了意想不到的结果。

7
00:00:53,840 --> 00:01:03,550
"What we found", said Dr Faulkner, "was an 80% increase in energy expenditure, just as a result of sitting in the bath for the course of an hour".
福克纳博士说：“我们发现，因为在浴缸里坐了一个小时，能量消耗就增加了80%。”

8
00:01:03,550 --> 00:01:13,300
You burn 140 calories - not as many perhaps as if you had worked out on an exercise bike, but the same number as if you had been on a brisk walk.
你燃烧了140卡路里——也许没有在健身单车上锻炼消耗的那么多，但和快走消耗的卡路里数量相同。

9
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:17,640
The real surprise, however, came in the blood sugar level results.
然而，真正令人惊讶的是血糖水平的结果。

10
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:27,940
The peak glucose output, the amount of blood sugar in the blood after a meal, was on average 10% lower after the bath compared to that after exercise.
餐后血液中的血糖量，即血糖峰值，泡澡后平均比运动后低10%。

11
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:40,110
Dr Faulkner's explanation for this phenomenon is that when you are in a hot bath, proteins, known as 'heat shock proteins' are released, which help divert the sugar from the bloodstream to the muscles.
福克纳博士对这一现象的解释是，当你泡在热水里时，被称为“热休克蛋白”的蛋白质会被释放出来，这些蛋白质有助于将糖分从血液中转移到肌肉中。

12
00:01:40,110 --> 00:01:45,490
It's important to keep blood sugar levels down to avoid damage to the arteries and nerves.
保持血糖水平低很重要，以避免对动脉和神经造成损害。

13
00:01:45,490 --> 00:01:49,360
Don't think, though, that you can hang up your trainers just yet!
不过，别以为你现在就可以把运动鞋收起来了！

14
00:01:49,360 --> 00:01:54,750
You should aim to do at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity exercise a week.
你应该目标是每周至少进行150分钟的中等强度运动。

15
00:01:54,750 --> 00:02:04,260
But, if you are one of those people who need to control their blood sugar levels - if you have type-2 diabetes for example or find it hard to exercise - why wait?
但是，如果你是那些需要控制血糖水平的人之一——比如你患有2型糖尿病，或者觉得运动很困难——那还等什么呢？

16
00:02:04,260 --> 00:02:07,000
Grab a towel and start running the hot tap!
拿条毛巾，打开热水龙头吧！
